<title>USA: NYCE cotton ends higher ahead of New Year holiday.</title>
<headline>NYCE cotton ends higher ahead of New Year holiday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>NYCE cotton futures ended the year firmer as players squared positions ahead of the New Year holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers attributed gains to profit-taking after four consecutive days of losses.</p>
<p>The most-active March contract ended 0.84 cent firmer at 75.15 cents per pound, traded 75.90 to 74.31 cents. The back months finished 0.83 higher to 0.75 lower.</p>
<p>Volume was estimated at 4,500 lots.</p>
<p>The NYCE will reopen Thursday.</p>
<p>--((Suzanne Rostler, New York Commodities 212-859-1646))</p>
